 "hypothesis": "H75-1 (EU3D-POE) + H73-BW BlockHoldout: Sliding-window 3-D Euler homogeneity structural-index deconvolution (N=0.5 fault contact vs N=2.0/2.5 equant plug), Morris (1996) WNW-ESE basement-strike slip/dilation criticality, and basin-thickness-normalized MT-thermal conduit columns capture blind/concealed Great Basin faults, while de-coupled multiplicative Product-of-Experts gating (P_scarp^0.35 * P_root^0.65) preserves 300-m scarp localization AND breaks Family-B LiDAR scarp convergence (<=70% sparse dot overlap across all 103 rasters).",
 "mechanism": "1) Vectorized 7x7 (700 m) 3-D Euler homogeneity solver with FFT downward vertical derivatives on isostatic gravity (N_c=0.5 vs N_p=2.0) and RTP magnetics (N_c=0.5 vs N_p=2.5), requiring horizontal apex offset <=250 m and crustal depth 50..3500 m. 2) Morris (1996) resolved normal dilation & shear tendency projected onto local basement gravity-contact normal under N65W-S65E Great Basin extension (az=115 deg). 3) High-pass surface conductance normalized by depth_to_base_surf (suppressing conductive playa fills) x heat-flow excess & Euler root. 4) Independent 4-quadrant LOQO OOF HGB experts P_scarp (28 Family-B/RBDT cols) and P_root (55 ACD+H34+H74+H75 cols) combined as P_scarp^0.35 * P_root^0.65 + B2 (d_cat > 2 px) submodular greedy_dots (37,654 dots).",
